Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-25
Subject: Call is_signed on secondfor loop types directly to avoid narrowing tenumdef to torddef (fpc 0.99)
License: expat

compiler/cg386flw.pas's `secondfor' computes whether the loop counter
is signed with:

    count_var_is_signed := is_signed(porddef(p^.t2^.resulttype));

That narrowing is unnecessary and wrong. `is_signed' already accepts a
plain `pdef' and handles both ordinal defs and enum defs. When the loop
counter type is an enum, the old cast first lies that the `tenumdef'
pointer is really a `torddef', and the translated bootstrap then
downcasts the object to the wrong dynamic type in step 5.

Fix: pass `p^.t2^.resulttype' directly to `is_signed'.

--- a/compiler/cg386flw.pas
+++ b/compiler/cg386flw.pas
@@ -232,7 +232,7 @@
 
          { produce start assignment }
          cleartempgen;
          secondpass(p^.left);
-         count_var_is_signed:=is_signed(porddef(p^.t2^.resulttype));
+         count_var_is_signed:=is_signed(p^.t2^.resulttype);
          if temptovalue then
              begin
               if p^.t2^.location.loc=LOC_CREGISTER then
